  <!-- ══ SECTION 3: PROGRAM OVERVIEW ══ -->
  <div class="section" id="program">
    <div class="section-hdr">
      <div class="badge-num">3</div>
      <h2>Program Overview — How It Works</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="overview-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What AMO Does</h3>
          <p>CMI's Advanced Marketing Orchestration (AMO) sends <strong>weekly NPI trigger files</strong> to EQ5 every Monday morning. Each file contains a list of specific HCPs and which journey stage they're at. EQ5 activates the corresponding Meta ads to those exact HCPs by Tuesday — deterministic, NPI-level targeting, not broad audience segments.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:10px">The trigger list shrinks and advances as HCPs move through the funnel: <strong>Education → Awareness → Consideration → Trial → Adoption</strong>. Lower-funnel HCPs see progressively more specific, conversion-focused messaging.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>EQ5's Role in the Program</h3>
          <p>EQ5 is the <strong>execution and optimization layer</strong> — receiving CMI's trigger lists, firing Meta campaigns to NPI-matched HCPs, managing creative rotation across touchpoints, and returning PLD (Placement Level Data) reports every Wednesday. That performance data feeds back into CMI's AMO orchestration loop to inform next-best-action decisions.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>Important:</strong> Within each AMO touchpoint group, EQ5's platform dynamically optimizes spend toward the best-performing assets. Impression and spend distribution across individual assets will vary — estimated figures show an equal split for planning purposes only.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="kpi-mini">
          <div class="kpi-m" style="border-top-color:var(--gold)"><div class="lbl">Total Budget (est.)</div><div class="val">$630K</div><div class="sub">Apr '26 – Mar '27</div></div>
          <div class="kpi-m"><div class="lbl">Total Impressions (est.)</div><div class="val">3.78M</div><div class="sub">Based on $166.76 CPM</div></div>
          <div class="kpi-m"><div class="lbl">HCP Audience</div><div class="val">43,603</div><div class="sub">40,144 reachable on Meta</div></div>
          <div class="kpi-m" style="border-top-color:var(--teal-l)"><div class="lbl">Match Rate</div><div class="val">92.1%</div><div class="sub">Best-in-class for HCP</div></div>
          <div class="kpi-m"><div class="lbl">Creative Assets</div><div class="val">35</div><div class="sub">Reel · Story · In-Feed</div></div>
          <div class="kpi-m" style="border-top-color:var(--amber)"><div class="lbl">AMO Launch Date</div><div class="val">Aug 15</div><div class="sub">2026 trigger files start</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="margin-top:10px">
          <h3>Weekly Operational Cadence</h3>
          <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0">
            <li style="padding:6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:11px;color:var(--mid)"><span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal);font-size:10px">MONDAY</span> — CMI uploads trigger file to SFTP</li>
            <li style="padding:6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:11px;color:var(--mid)"><span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal);font-size:10px">TUESDAY</span> — EQ5 activates Meta campaigns to matched HCPs</li>
            <li style="padding:6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:11px;color:var(--mid)"><span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal);font-size:10px">WEDNESDAY</span> — EQ5 returns PLD report (Mon–Sun coverage)</li>
            <li style="padding:6px 0;font-size:11px;color:var(--mid)"><span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-weight:600;color:var(--teal);font-size:10px">ONGOING</span> — CMI uses data to update next-best-action triggers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ══ SECTION 4: OPEN ALIGNMENT ITEMS ══ -->
